```verilog
module TopModule (
    input  a,
    input  b,
    output out_and,
    output out_or,
    output out_xor,
    output out_nand,
    output out_nor,
    output out_xnor,
    output out_anotb
);

    assign out_and   = a & b;
    assign out_or    = a | b;
    assign out_xor   = a ^ b;
    assign out_nand  = ~(a & b);
    assign out_nor   = ~(a | b);
    assign out_xnor  = ~(a ^ b);
    assign out_anotb = a & ~b;

endmodule
```

This module uses continuous assignments to implement each of the 7 logic gates combinationally:
- `out_and`: AND gate
- `out_or`: OR gate
- `out_xor`: XOR gate
- `out_nand`: NAND gate (inverted AND)
- `out_nor`: NOR gate (inverted OR)
- `out_xnor`: XNOR gate (inverted XOR)
- `out_anotb`: AND with inverted b (a and-not b)
